Luza is an all-inclusive consulting company focused on talent, tech and innovation. We exist to elevate companies and humans all around the world, making change, from the inside to the outside.

We believe that technology + human kindness positively impacts every community around the world. Our approach is simple, we see a world without borders, and believe in equal opportunities. We are guided by our core principles of spreading positivity, good energy and promote equality and care for others.

Our hiring process is unique! People are selected by their value, education, talent and personality. We dont present ethnicity, religion, national origin, age, gender, sexual orientation or identity.

Its time to burst the bubble, and we will do it together!

What You'll do:


Translate business requirements into scalable Power BI and Microsoft Fabric solutions;
Design and maintain Power BI reports, dashboards and enterprise semantic models using market best pratices;
Develop metrics and KPI frameworks using advanced DAX;
Manage Power BI Service workspaces, Apps, gateways, refreshes, semantic models and deployment pipelines;
Implement Row-Level Security and appropriate access controls;
Optimize reports and semantic models for performance and scalability;
Design Fabric solutions using OneLake, Lakehouse, Warehouse and Data Factory pipelines;
Ingest and transform data from SQL, APIs, cloud platforms, and flat files;
Support governance, data quality, lineage, monitoring, testing, and release management;
Collaborate with technical teams, review solutions and mentor other analysts or developers;
Hybrid work model;



Who You Are:


More than 3 years of experience;
Advanced hands-on experience with Power BI Desktop, Power BI Service, DAX and semantic modelling;
Strong SQL and Power Query/M skills, with proven experience applying star-schema, fact and dimension modelling;
Experience managing enterprise Power BI environments, including Workspaces, Apps, gateways and Deployment Pipelines;
Experience implementing Row-Level Security and applying BI governance, security and enterprise delivery standards;
Hands-on Microsoft Fabric experience, particularly with OneLake, Lakehouse, Warehouse and Data Factory;
Proven ability to troubleshoot and optimize Power BI and Fabric solutions for performance and scalability;
Strong communication, stakeholder management and problem-solving skills;
Fluent in Portuguese and English;



Desirable Experience:


Direct Lake, composite models, XMLA, Tabular Editor, TMDL or calculation groups;
DAX Studio, VertiPaq Analyzer or other performance-tuning tools;
Microsoft Purview, Fabric capacity management, Power BI REST APIs or automation;
CI/CD, source control, Azure data services or large-scale international deployments.



What you'll get:


Wage according to candidate's professional experience;
Remote Work whenever possible;
Delivery of work equipment adjusted to the performance of functions;
Benefits plan;
And others.



Work together with expert teams on projects of large magnitude and intensity, long term together with our clients, all leaders in their industries.

Are you ready to step into a diverse and inclusive world with us?

Together we will promote uniquess!
